// A NEW tier-1 defect, found and closed in the same round (2026-09-09g) by
// varying the SHAPE past what the pricing round's prompt named. `&&ref a` over
// a `&&i64` scrutinee: the `&`-pattern spends TWO layers, so sema binds
// `a : &i64` — one layer FEWER than the scrutinee value carries. The old match
// door aliased the scrutinee unconditionally whenever it was pointer-
// represented, so `a` held the address of the outer reference and `*a` read a
// POINTER as an i64: exit 1, a silent wrong answer on the base binary
// 58fd3c9773b9c475 43, with no diagnostic. Neither the crude nor the refined
// arm the pricing round priced moved it — both gated on `&`-depth 0 — which is
// why deciding by the binder's sema TYPE rather than by a depth counter is the
// fix that covers the class in both directions.
// The fail half one token away is fail/refpat_refbind_depth2_type.
package refpat_refbind_depth2;
use logos.std.fmt;
fn main() -> i32 {
    let n: i64 = 6i64;
    let r: &i64 = &n;
    let rr: &&i64 = &r;
    match rr {
        &&ref a => {
            println!("a={}", *a);
            if *a != 6i64 { return 1i32; }
            return 0i32;
        }
    }
}
